UID:graner-creative-grants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Deadline: Graner Creative Grants 2027: Residencies for Dance and Li
 ve Arts (Barcelona)
DESCRIPTION:Graner\, Barcelona's centre for dance and live arts creation wi
 thin the city council's Creative Factories Network\, managed by Mercat de 
 les Flors with the Catalan dance professionals' associations APDC and ACPD
 C\, opens its 2027 call for residency grants supporting creation and resea
 rch projects taking place between January and December 2027. EIGHT CATEGOR
 IES: Associated Artist (1 place\, EUR 6\,000 per year for 2027 and 2028\, 
 for Catalonia-based artists who associate with the centre for two years\, 
 with a creative residency of up to six weeks)\; Creation (3 places\, EUR 6
 \,000\, local and national artists developing projects leading to a produc
 tion\, up to five weeks)\; Barcelona Crea Research (2 places\, EUR 6\,000\
 , local researchers and artists in the initial stages of artistic research
  with body\, movement and choreographic thinking as its axes)\; Barcelona 
 Crea Critical Thinking (1 place\, EUR 6\,000\, theoretical\, critical or d
 iscursive projects on dance and the live arts)\; International (1 place\, 
 EUR 3\,000\, for researchers\, artists and collectives based outside Spain
  without a direct connection to the Catalan or Spanish context\, two to fo
 ur weeks\; applying here excludes all other categories)\; Stage Research (
 1 place\, EUR 3\,000\, research centred on lighting\, sound\, video or sce
 nography\, with technical studio time and support sessions)\; Emerging Art
 ists (2 places\, EUR 3\,000\, endowment topped up with EUR 1\,700 contribu
 ted by Can Gassol in Mataro\, where part of the residency takes place)\; a
 nd Practical Methodologies (1 place\, EUR 3\,000). WHAT YOU GET: on top of
  the grant\, a workspace agreed per project\, possible technical residency
 \, shared desk and facilities\, artistic support and possible specialised 
 mentoring\, participation in Graner's labs\, workshops and seminars\, comm
 unication support\, and covered national and European travel to the two an
 nual APLEC gatherings. ELIGIBILITY: natural persons\, legal persons and gr
 oups with or without legal personality\; applicants may apply to at most t
 wo categories (International is mutually exclusive) and can receive only o
 ne grant. Barcelona Crea categories require a demonstrated connection to B
 arcelona or its metropolitan area and carry municipal-grant incompatibilit
 y rules. NOTE: structural renovation works run at Graner throughout 2027 a
 nd may affect studio use. APPLICATION: free\, via the category-specific fo
 rms on the Mercat de les Flors website\; an English-language bases PDF det
 ails each category. DEADLINE: 29 September 2026 at 14:00 Catalan time (12:
 00 UTC).\n\nOrganisation: El Graner Fabrica de Creacio\, managed by Mercat
  de les Flors\nLocation: Graner\, Barcelona\, Spain (with part of the Emer
 ging Artists residencies at Can Gassol\, Mataro). Most categories are for 
 local and national artists\; one International category is reserved for ar
 tists based outside Spain.\nAward: 12 grants totalling EUR 57\,000. EUR 6\
 ,000 per project for Associated Artist (1 place\, EUR 6\,000 each for 2027
  and 2028)\, Creation (3 places)\, Barcelona Crea Research (2) and Barcelo
 na Crea Critical Thinking (1). EUR 3\,000 per project for Stage Research (
 1)\, International (1)\, Emerging Artists (2\, endowment topped up with EU
 R 1\,700 from Can Gassol) and Practical Methodologies (1). Plus workspace\
 , possible technical residency\, artistic support and covered travel to th
 e two annual APLEC gatherings. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies 
 between January and December 2027\, typically up to four to six weeks\, no
 t necessarily consecutive\, depending on category. The Associated Artist c
 ommits for two years (2027-2028).\n\nMore: https://mercatflors.cat/en/beca
 /2027-call-for-proposals-for-creative-grants-el-graner-fabrica-de-creacio/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://mercatflors.cat/en/beca/2027-call-for-proposals-for-creative-gr
 ants-el-graner-fabrica-de-creacio/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Graner\, Barcelona\, Spain (with part of the Emerging Artists resi
 dencies at Can Gassol\, Mataro). Most categories are for local and nationa
 l artists\; one International category is reserved for artists based outsi
 de Spain.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:camargo-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Camargo Fellowship 2027-2028 for Artists\, Scholars and T
 hinkers (Cassis\, France)
DESCRIPTION:The Camargo Foundation invites artists\, scholars and thinkers 
 to its flagship Core Fellowship: a ten-week self-directed residency on its
  clifftop campus overlooking the Mediterranean in Cassis\, France\, dedica
 ted to research\, experimentation and interdisciplinary exchange. Curators
  apply under the Thinkers category\, which covers accomplished professiona
 ls and practitioners in cultural and creative fields who are professionall
 y engaged in critical thought\, including curators\, critics and journalis
 ts\; projects should engage theoretical\, artistic or societal questions. 
 WHAT YOU GET: a stipend of EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 total)\, basic tra
 nsportation funding\, and a furnished apartment with an equipped kitchen o
 n campus. Fourteen fellowships are awarded per year: seven for artists and
  seven for scholars and thinkers. RESIDENCY PERIODS: Fall 2027 (8 Septembe
 r to 17 November 2027) or Spring 2028 (23 February to 4 May 2028). ELIGIBI
 LITY: artists in visual arts\, performance\, writing\, film\, music or mul
 tidisciplinary work with at least 5 years of professional practice\; schol
 ars holding or pursuing a PhD focused on French and Francophone cultures o
 r cross-cultural Mediterranean studies\; and thinkers as described above. 
 APPLICATION: via Submittable with a 100-word proposal summary\, a 1\,200-w
 ord proposal narrative\, a 300-word rationale for Camargo\, a 300-word car
 eer-stage rationale\, a CV (max 3 pages)\, work samples and two references
 . NOTE: the foundation has announced that this is the final Fellowship sel
 ected through a public open call until further notice\; a new selection pr
 ocess begins in July 2027\, making this the last chance to apply directly.
 \n\nOrganisation: Camargo Foundation\nLocation: Camargo Foundation campus\
 , Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.\nAward: EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 to
 tal for the ten-week residency)\, plus basic travel funding and a furnishe
 d apartment with equipped kitchen on the Camargo campus. 14 fellowships pe
 r year: 7 for artists and 7 for scholars and thinkers. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Ten weeks\, either 8 September to 17 November 2027 or 23 Febru
 ary to 4 May 2028.\n\nMore: https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fello
 wship-2026-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Camargo Foundation campus\, Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sim-residency-nordic-baltic-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: SÍM Residency: Funded Nordic-Baltic Residency January-Fe
 bruary 2027 (Reykjavík)
DESCRIPTION:The SÍM Residency in Reykjavík announces its January to Febru
 ary 2027 funded residency for four artists from the Nordic-Baltic region. 
 The two-month program invites multidisciplinary artists interested in arti
 stic research and production addressing sustainability\, ecology\, social 
 equality and Nordic cultural narratives\; artists from visual arts\, perfo
 rmance\, sound\, digital media and research are encouraged to apply. Parti
 cipants develop individual projects while engaging in studio visits with a
  curator\, discussions\, public open studios and talks\, closing with an e
 xhibition or public presentation at Seljavegur 32. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 2\,00
 0 stipend\, EUR 600 travel\, EUR 500 materials\, accommodation with a priv
 ate bedroom\, a private studio\, orientation\, presentation on the SÍM we
 bsite and social media\, and connections to local workshops (sound recordi
 ng\, Fab Lab\, ceramics\, textile\, darkroom). Funded by the Nordic-Baltic
  Mobility Programme for Culture\; artists are encouraged to seek top-up fu
 nding from their home arts councils if needed. ELIGIBILITY: a permanent ad
 dress in the Nordic countries (Denmark\, Finland\, the Faroe Islands\, Gre
 enland\, Norway\, Sweden\, Åland) or Baltic states (Estonia\, Latvia\, Li
 thuania)\, any nationality\; artists living in Iceland are excluded. A BA 
 in visual arts or a similar field is required\, or equivalent professional
  experience\; candidates without one may apply with a letter of recommenda
 tion from a curator\, museum or gallery. Candidates must commit to the ful
 l 3 January to 28 February 2027 period\, communicate in English\, attend a
 ll meetings and events\, participate in the final exhibition\, and have th
 eir project documented on the SÍM website. APPLICATION: a 400-word projec
 t proposal toward the theme\, stating specific interests\, why the residen
 cy matters for the applicant's career now\, openness to collaboration\, an
 d environmentally responsible methods and material choices. CONDITIONS: no
  overnight guests in the residency apartment and no pets\; artists are not
  required to leave artwork behind. DEADLINE: 1 October 2026.\n\nOrganisati
 on: SÍM Residency (Association of Icelandic Visual Artists)\nLocation: Se
 ljavegur 32\, Reykjavík\, Iceland. Open to artists with a permanent addre
 ss in Denmark\, Finland\, the Faroe Islands\, Greenland\, Norway\, Sweden\
 , Åland\, Estonia\, Latvia or Lithuania\, regardless of nationality. Arti
 sts living in Iceland are explicitly excluded. The apartment is on the sec
 ond floor\, staircase only\, no elevator.\nAward: EUR 2\,000 stipend for t
 he whole period\, EUR 600 travel costs and EUR 500 material costs\, plus a
 ccommodation (private bedroom\, shared kitchen and living spaces) and a pr
 ivate studio. Funded by the Nordic-Baltic Mobility Programme for Culture. 
 Four places.\nDuration: Two months\, 3 January to 28 February 2027. Full a
 ttendance is required\; shorter periods are not granted.\n\nMore: https://
 www.sim-residency.info/ncp-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://www.sim-residency.info/ncp-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Seljavegur 32\, Reykjavík\, Iceland. Open to artists with a perma
 nent address in Denmark\, Finland\, the Faroe Islands\, Greenland\, Norway
 \, Sweden\, Åland\, Estonia\, Latvia or Lithuania\, regardless of nationa
 lity. Artists living in Iceland are explicitly excluded. The apartment is 
 on the second floor\, staircase only\, no elevator.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ernest-albert-invitational-reflective-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261014
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261015
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ernest Albert Invitational 2027: Reflective Residency at 
 Cas-co x Kunsthal Mechelen
DESCRIPTION:Cas-co and Kunsthal Mechelen invite Belgium-based emerging cura
 tors\, writers\, critics\, researchers\, art historians and research-based
  practitioners to apply for the Ernest Albert Invitational 2027\, a four-m
 onth Reflective Residency at Cas-co in Leuven within the Off the Grid prog
 ramme. The Reflective Resident joins the four artists of Cas-co's Artistic
  Development Residency from 14 January to 14 May 2027\, developing an inde
 pendent research trajectory while closely following the questions\, proces
 ses and conversations emerging within the group. Reflection is understood 
 as an active practice: creating connections\, introducing perspectives\, a
 sking questions and generating new contexts around artistic work. The resi
 dency culminates in a Reflective contribution to the public programme of t
 he group exhibition at Kunsthal Mechelen\, 4 June to 29 August 2027\, cura
 ted by Jessica Meuleman (Kunsthal Mechelen)\, Zuzanna Rachowska and Arthur
  Cordier (Cas-co). SUPPORT: EUR 1\,100 artist fee per month\, EUR 120 tran
 sportation allowance per month\, and a one-time production budget of EUR 6
 00 (EUR 5\,480 total including VAT). ELIGIBILITY: Belgium-based\; priority
  goes to applicants early in their careers\, with limited institutional ac
 cess\, or developing interdisciplinary research practices around contempor
 ary art. HOW TO APPLY: one PDF (max 10 MB) with a description of your prac
 tice\, a proposal\, CV and portfolio\, via the online application form (Go
 ogle Form linked from the call page). Jury meets 26 October 2026\; selecti
 on announced 4 November 2026. Queries to arthur[at]cas-co.be. Deadline 14 
 October 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Cas-co\, Leuven and Kunsthal M
 echelen\nLocation: Cas-co\, Leuven\, Belgium\, within the Off the Grid pro
 gramme\, with the closing exhibition at Kunsthal Mechelen. Open only to Be
 lgium-based applicants.\nAward: EUR 5\,480 total including VAT: an artist 
 fee of EUR 1\,100 per month\, a transportation allowance of EUR 120 per mo
 nth\, and a one-time production budget of EUR 600. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Four months\, 14 January to 14 May 2027\, culminating in a contrib
 ution to the group exhibition's public programme at Kunsthal Mechelen from
  4 June to 29 August 2027\n\nMore: https://cas-co.be/nieuws/cas-coxkunstha
 lmechelen-artist-open-call-deadline-28-10-26-2?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cas-co.be/nieuws/cas-coxkunsthalmechelen-artist-open-call-deadl
 ine-28-10-26-2?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cas-co\, Leuven\, Belgium\, within the Off the Grid programme\, wi
 th the closing exhibition at Kunsthal Mechelen. Open only to Belgium-based
  applicants.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:effea-call-5-festival-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: EFFEA Call #5: European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artis
 ts
DESCRIPTION:The European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artists (EFFEA)\, an i
 nitiative of the European Festivals Association co-funded by the European 
 Union\, opens its fifth call: 50 residencies for 50 emerging artists (indi
 viduals\, groups or collectives) hosted by partnerships of around 150 fest
 ivals\, each led by one leading festival with a minimum of two partner fes
 tivals from different eligible countries. TWO CATEGORIES: EFFEA Discovery\
 , 40 grants of EUR 8\,000 for artists at the early stages of their careers
  with strong potential to break through internationally\; and EFFEA Spring
 board\, 10 grants of EUR 15\,000 for artists already established in their 
 own country and ready to develop their careers internationally. A Discover
 y residency includes a work-in-progress presentation at the leading festiv
 al\, a workshop with programmers from each partner festival\, a short film
  about the residency\, and participation in the EFFEA Intake and Outtake S
 eminars\; a Springboard residency includes at least three presentations of
  the production result (leading festival plus each partner festival) and a
  live masterclass by the artist in at least three countries. DISCIPLINES: 
 architecture\, ballet\, contemporary dance\, circus\, design and applied a
 rts\, digital arts\, film\, folklore and folk arts\, heritage\, interdisci
 plinary\, literature\, music\, opera\, street art\, theatre\, photography 
 and video\, puppetry\, sculpture\, painting. WHO APPLIES: the leading fest
 ival submits the application online via the EFFEA website and proposes the
  artists\; festivals must be registered on FestivalFinder.eu and have held
  at least one edition. Artists may be of any age and must have nationality
  or legal residence in an eligible country. Emerging is defined by novelty
  to programmers and audiences\, not by age. FINANCES: minimum 80 percent o
 f the grant goes to artist costs\; own contributions of EUR 1\,000 (Discov
 ery) or EUR 2\,000 (Springboard) are deducted from the grant\; in-kind cos
 ts are capped at 10 percent. TIMELINE: evaluation in November 2026\, resul
 ts by email in December 2026\, residencies between 1 January and 31 Decemb
 er 2027 (Intake Seminar 26 January 2027\, Outtake Seminar 21 September 202
 7). Deadline 3 November 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: European Festi
 vals Association (EFA)\nLocation: Residencies hosted by festival partnersh
 ips of at least three festivals from three eligible countries (most of Eur
 ope plus Tunisia and Ukraine). Leading festivals and artists must be based
  in an eligible country\; festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\
 , Turkey and the UK may join as partner festivals only\, and artists from 
 those countries may also be proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing th
 e artists\; artists cannot apply directly.\nAward: 50 residency grants: 40
  Discovery grants of EUR 8\,000 (for artists at an early career stage) and
  10 Springboard grants of EUR 15\,000 (for artists established at home and
  ready to break through internationally). A minimum of 80 percent of the g
 rant must cover costs incurred by the artists (fees\, travel\, accommodati
 on\, subsistence). An own contribution of EUR 1\,000 (Discovery) or EUR 2\
 ,000 (Springboard) is deducted from the paid grant. No application fee.\nD
 uration: Residencies implemented between 1 January and 31 December 2027\, 
 co-produced by one leading festival and at least two partner festivals\n\n
 More: https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residencies hosted by festival partnerships of at least three fest
 ivals from three eligible countries (most of Europe plus Tunisia and Ukrai
 ne). Leading festivals and artists must be based in an eligible country\; 
 festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\, Turkey and the UK may jo
 in as partner festivals only\, and artists from those countries may also b
 e proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing the artists\; artists cannot
  apply directly.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:can-serrat-visual-art-residency-full-grants-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:Deadline: Can Serrat: Visual Art Residency 2027 full grants (El Bru
 c\, Catalonia)
DESCRIPTION:Can Serrat is a long-running international residency in a forme
 r winery in El Bruc\, at the foot of the Montserrat massif about an hour f
 rom Barcelona. Its 2027 visual art open call is aimed at visual and multid
 isciplinary artists of all career levels and nationalities\, with the resi
 dency window running 2 August to 12 December 2027. THE FUNDED PLACES: one 
 full grant with honoraries\, comprising a EUR 2\,000 honorarium (subject t
 o public funding) and a private room at Can Serrat for six consecutive wee
 ks from 2 August 2027\; and one full grant with shared accommodation for o
 ne month in October 2027. Both full grants include two weekly communal din
 ners and basic food supplies (coffee\, tea\, condiments\, select dry goods
 ). ALL RESIDENTS additionally get studio and workspace access\, shared fac
 ilities\, monthly public presentations\, an unlimited public transport pas
 s\, publication of the project in Can Serrat's digital archive and visibil
 ity through its channels. POST-RESIDENCY: a EUR 3\,000 visual arts product
 ion grant and return grants (one-month return stays) are available to 2027
  residents in December 2027. NOTE ON THE REST OF THE CALL: the same applic
 ation also allocates around 20 partial grants\, where residents pay EUR 1\
 ,130 per month for a shared room or EUR 1\,745 per month for a private roo
 m (both with the dinners and basics included)\, or EUR 305 per month for s
 tudio-only without accommodation\; only the two full grants are fully fund
 ed. APPLICATIONS: window 1 to 23 September 2026 via the open call page. No
  application fee stated.\n\nOrganisation: Can Serrat International Art Res
 idency\nLocation: Can Serrat\, El Bruc\, at the foot of Montserrat near Ba
 rcelona\, Catalonia\, Spain. Open to visual and multidisciplinary artists 
 of all career levels and nationalities.\nAward: Two fully funded places: o
 ne full grant with a EUR 2\,000 honorarium (subject to public funding) plu
 s a private room for six consecutive weeks from 2 August 2027\, and one fu
 ll grant with shared accommodation for one month in October 2027\; both in
 clude two weekly communal dinners and basic food supplies. A EUR 3\,000 pr
 oduction grant and return grants are additionally available to 2027 reside
 nts in December 2027. No application fee stated. The same call also offers
  around 20 partial grants where residents pay EUR 1\,130 per month (shared
  room)\, EUR 1\,745 per month (private room) or EUR 305 per month (studio 
 only).\nDuration: Full grant with honorarium: six consecutive weeks from 2
  August 2027. Second full grant: one month in October 2027. The overall 20
 27 residency window runs 2 August to 12 December 2027\; partial-grant stay
 s are minimum one month.\n\nMore: https://canserrat.org/es/en-visual-art-r
 esidency-open-call-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://canserrat.org/es/en-visual-art-residency-open-call-2027?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Can Serrat\, El Bruc\, at the foot of Montserrat near Barcelona\, 
 Catalonia\, Spain. Open to visual and multidisciplinary artists of all car
 eer levels and nationalities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ctm-resynthesising-traditional-at-the-extreme-2027@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: CTM Festival: Resynthesising the Traditional 2027 Artisti
 c Lab (At the Extreme)
DESCRIPTION:Resynthesising the Traditional is CTM Festival's long-term init
 iative co-curated by Stas Sharifulla\, taking resynthesis (the computer-mu
 sic method of analysing a sound to extract its components) as a metaphor f
 or critically engaging with tradition and heritage\, against conservative 
 views of culture as frozen and untouchable. The artistic lab at its heart 
 is an open toolbox for artists connecting to the traditional outside exoti
 cisation\, cultural essentialism and uneven power dynamics. THEME\, AT THE
  EXTREME: this edition invites artists and practice-based researchers whos
 e work examines the ethical\, aesthetic and political implications of trad
 itions entangled with extremity: intensity\, transgression\, transformatio
 n\, marginality\, outsiderness\, endurance\, conflict and excess. The call
  explicitly looks past the usual noise\, violence and loud-popular-music t
 ropes and past masculine codings of the extreme\, toward current queer and
  feminist reframings\, treating extremity as a relational condition\, chos
 en or imposed\, produced between majoritarian centres and their minoritari
 an outsides. Guiding questions include what it means to follow a tradition
  to its extreme consequences\, who is allowed to push tradition to its lim
 its and whose practices get framed as inauthentic or dangerous\, what it m
 eans to practise tradition under war\, displacement\, repression or ecolog
 ical crisis\, and how traditions might offer ways of inhabiting extreme ti
 mes. Preference goes to work engaging technological\, bodily\, aesthetic a
 nd theoretical forms at that intersection\, especially in unexpected or ra
 rely recognised ways. WHAT HAPPENS: theory and practice workshops from the
  co-hosts with individual and group exercises\, closed 15 to 20 minute ora
 l presentations by each participant\, a solo public performance or present
 ation (15 to 20 minutes) at a free-entry event\, inputs from specialists s
 uch as artists\, researchers and technologists\, guided individual and gro
 up sonic improvisations\, field trips and site visits\, and feedback sessi
 ons with the co-hosts and curators. AFTERWARDS: participants may propose n
 ew artistic work or research\, solo or in collaborations formed at the lab
 \, to the artistic team\; selected works are shortlisted\, and up to two a
 re commissioned and presented at CTM in January/February 2028. ELIGIBILITY
 : an existing practice tied to (re)connecting with traditional ideas and s
 ounds through a contemporary lens and how that overlaps with the extreme\,
  plus clear ideas or questions about the next step you want to take. Appro
 aches may be technological\, instrument-focused\, compositional\, aestheti
 c\, research-oriented or otherwise. Working knowledge of English is recomm
 ended\, and any concerns about that can be flagged in the form. Up to six 
 participants are selected by co-hosts Karina Utomo (extreme metal vocalist
 \, composer and collaborative artist) and Luigi Monteanni (sound researche
 r and ethnomusicologist completing a PhD at SOAS on extreme metal in Bandu
 ng). The lab is a time-intensive full-day commitment and participants must
  agree to give the short public performance. APPLY through the form with a
  portfolio link (PDF\, max 10 pages\, public access\, works from the last 
 five years\, text kept minimal) and a link to a specific audio track or se
 ction (max five minutes) that best represents your current practice. CTM a
 sks that AI support rather than replace your own voice in the application.
  TIMELINE: deadline 28 September 2026\; participants announced mid to late
  October 2026. Questions to resynth@ctm-festival.de.\n\nOrganisation: CTM 
 Festival\, co-curated by Stas Sharifulla\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany. Open
  to artists worldwide\; solo artists and projects only.\nAward: Travel bud
 get of up to EUR 300 per person\, plus accommodation and catering for the 
 duration of the lab and a festival pass to CTM 2027 events. Visa fees are 
 supported where required\, and letters of invitation are provided for visa
  or funding applications. NO artist fee or stipend for the lab itself. Aft
 erwards\, up to two new works arising from the lab may be commissioned and
  presented at CTM Festival in January/February 2028. No application fee.\n
 Duration: Seven days: arrival 24 January\, lab 26 to 31 January 2027 (10:0
 0 to 19:00 daily)\, public presentations 26 January\, departure 1 February
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/resyn
 thesising-the-traditional-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/resynthesising-the
 -traditional-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. Open to artists worldwide\; solo artists and pro
 jects only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:delfina-gulbenkian-artists-portugal-lusophone-africa-2027@artificialnou
 veau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Deadline: Delfina Foundation x Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation: Open
  Call for Artists from Portugal and Portuguese-Speaking African Nations (L
 ondon residency)
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation (UK Bran
 ch)\, Delfina Foundation welcomes applications from contemporary visual ar
 tists from Portugal\, Angola\, Mozambique\, Guinea-Bissau\, Cape Verde and
  Sao Tome and Principe for a London residency from 28 June to 17 September
  2027\, during Delfina's open summer season dedicated to independent resea
 rch. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be born in one of the six eligible count
 ries (individuals currently based in the UK are not eligible)\; be seeking
  to develop their practice through research\; be able to explain how an in
 ternational residency may benefit their career development and local netwo
 rks\; and be proficient in English (the interview is conducted in English)
 . Collectives and duos are advised to put forth one member to be in reside
 nce. THE PROGRAMME: alongside time and space to develop their work\, resid
 ents get guided visits to museums\, galleries\, non-profits\, artist-run s
 paces and studios\, plus trips to institutions outside London\; opportunit
 ies to meet artists\, curators\, academics and researchers through organis
 ed presentations\, studio visits\, events and meals\; professional develop
 ment including presentations and crits\, portfolio reviews and mentoring\;
  and collaborative exchange between residents through informal gatherings 
 and meals. APPLY via the online application form (Cognito Forms\, save-and
 -resume supported)\; Delfina strongly recommends reading the Guidance Note
 s document carefully before starting. All applicants notified by mid-Novem
 ber 2026. Deadline Sunday 4 October 2026\, 23:59 BST.\n\nOrganisation: Del
 fina Foundation\, in partnership with the Calouste Gulbenkian Foundation (
 UK Branch)\nLocation: Delfina Foundation\, 29-31 Catherine Place\, London\
 , UK. Applicants must be born in Portugal\, Angola\, Mozambique\, Guinea-B
 issau\, Cape Verde or Sao Tome and Principe\; individuals currently based 
 in the UK are not eligible.\nAward: Twelve-week fully funded residency: a 
 return economy-class flight\, airport transfers in the UK\, reimbursement 
 of visa fees if required\, a living allowance of GBP 40 per day\, a materi
 als budget of GBP 1\,200\, a travel pass for London's public transport net
 work\, and a single bedroom with a desk at Delfina Foundation\, a house ho
 sting up to eight residents with shared bathrooms\, laundry rooms\, kitche
 n\, library and dining room. No application fee.\nDuration: Twelve weeks\,
  28 June to 17 September 2027\, during Delfina's open summer 2027 residenc
 y season.\n\nMore: https://www.delfinafoundation.com/open-calls/current/op
 en-call-for-artists-from-portugal-or-portugese-speaking-african-nations/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.delfinafoundation.com/open-calls/current/open-call-for-arti
 sts-from-portugal-or-portugese-speaking-african-nations/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Delfina Foundation\, 29-31 Catherine Place\, London\, UK. Applican
 ts must be born in Portugal\, Angola\, Mozambique\, Guinea-Bissau\, Cape V
 erde or Sao Tome and Principe\; individuals currently based in the UK are 
 not eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) runs this r
 esidency with Videotage\, a Hong Kong-based non-profit media arts institut
 ion specialising in the promotion\, presentation\, creation and preservati
 on of moving image and media art in all forms and languages. The Fund is r
 ecruiting one Netherlands-based designer\, maker or observer working in di
 gital culture to spend two or three months at Videotage's studio space in 
 Hong Kong in 2027\, conducting research\, broadening their network\, devel
 oping new work inspired by Hong Kong\, and presenting their findings or co
 mpleted works. The residency encourages crossovers and experimentation\, g
 iving the participant space to explore new methodologies\, widen their cre
 ative practice and produce work that pushes the boundaries of digital cult
 ure\, with a focus on social and urban dynamics. The 2027 edition takes th
 e technological 'black box' phenomenon as its starting point and invites t
 he resident to respond to that theme within the context of Videotage. ELIG
 IBILITY: you are an individual designer\, maker or observer within the fie
 ld of digital culture\; you are established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, B
 onaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the N
 etherlands)\; you are registered in the business register of the Dutch Cha
 mber of Commerce (KvK) or another business register within the Kingdom of 
 the Netherlands\; and you have had a professional practice in the creative
  industry for at least four years. NOT open to duos\, collectives or coope
 rative ventures\, nor to designers and makers who receive a grant during t
 he work period under the Talent Development Grant Scheme\, the Open Call S
 elf-taught Designer or the Open Call Emerging Design Practices ABCSSS. Not
 e that accepting this open call means you cannot apply to those schemes an
 d open calls in 2027. FUNDING: EUR 5\,000 for two months or EUR 6\,500 for
  three months\, covering travel\, insurance\, living expenses\, compensati
 on for time invested and material and transport costs\; accommodation\, st
 udio use and Videotage's facilitation are covered separately by the Fund. 
 Submit your proposal to the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026
 \, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Cre
 ative Industries Fund NL) in collaboration with Videotage\, Hong Kong\nLoc
 ation: Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must be
  established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint 
 Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a
  business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\,0
 00 for a two-month residency or EUR 6\,500 for a three-month residency\, p
 aid by the Creative Industries Fund NL to cover travel\, insurance\, livin
 g expenses\, compensation for time invested\, and material and transport c
 osts. Accommodation\, use of the studio space and facilitation by Videotag
 e are covered directly by the Fund on top of this. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Two or three months in 2027 (spring 2027)\; state your preferred p
 eriod in the application.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gra
 nts/open-call-videotage?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must b
 e established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint
  Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in 
 a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ars-biologica-artxscience-residency-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ars Biologica ArtXScience Residency 2027-2028 (Ars Electr
 onica x Ceske Budejovice ECoC 2028)
DESCRIPTION:A fully funded art-science residency from Ars Electronica and C
 eske Budejovice\, European Capital of Culture 2028\, exploring how art and
  science can collaborate on urgent environmental challenges: climate emerg
 ence\, sustainable agriculture\, geoengineering\, permaculture\, water res
 ource management\, and the broader ecological impacts on local communities
 . Selected residents work in direct collaboration with local scientists in
  Ceske Budejovice. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, designers\, creatives and arti
 st collectives with more than 5 years of professional creative practice an
 d documented interdisciplinary work\; experience in community engagement a
 nd science collaborations is essential\; applicants must be 18+\, of any n
 ationality\, and legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. WHAT YOU G
 ET: a EUR 24\,000 package (EUR 6\,000 artist fee\, up to EUR 15\,000 produ
 ction\, up to EUR 3\,000 travel and subsistence) plus one month of housing
  covered separately\; two winners are selected. STRUCTURE: the residency r
 uns January 2027 to April 2028\, with a required on-site stay of up to one
  month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/September 2027\
 , and a March 2028 stay for festival installation\, exhibition and deinsta
 llation. HOW TO APPLY: online form with project title\, a written proposal
  of max 250 words\, a scientific direction statement (max 100 words)\, art
 istic vision (max 100 words)\, community connection plan (max 100 words)\,
  a super short pitch (3 to 30 words)\, 3 to 7 images\, an optional 1-minut
 e video\, a portfolio link and contact information. Two-round selection (o
 nline application then interview)\; winners notified by November 2026. Dea
 dline 28 September 2026 at midnight CET.\n\nOrganisation: Ars Electronica 
 and Ceske Budejovice - European Capital of Culture 2028\nLocation: Ceske B
 udejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any nationality aged 18+
  who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Required on-site s
 tays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/
 September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibition and deinstal
 lation.\nAward: EUR 24\,000 total package per winner: EUR 6\,000 artist fe
 e\, up to EUR 15\,000 production budget\, and up to EUR 3\,000 for travel\
 , accommodation and subsistence\, plus a separate budget covering one mont
 h of housing in Ceske Budejovice. Two positions available. Free to apply.\
 nDuration: January 2027 to April 2028\, with on-site blocks in early 2027 
 and March 2028\n\nMore: https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars
 -biologica-art-science-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars-biologica-art-scienc
 e-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ceske Budejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any natio
 nality aged 18+ who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Req
 uired on-site stays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional 
 stay in August/September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibiti
 on and deinstallation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:american-academy-berlin-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Berlin: Berlin Prize Fellowship 2027-
 28
DESCRIPTION:The American Academy in Berlin is an independent\, nonprofit in
 stitute for advanced study in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\, la
 w\, journalism and public policy\, whose primary mission is to strengthen 
 the cultural and intellectual ties between the United States and Germany. 
 Each year\, after a rigorous selection process\, the Academy awards roughl
 y two dozen semester-long Berlin Prize fellowships to individuals who demo
 nstrate excellence in their fields. DISCIPLINES: applications are welcome 
 across the humanities\, social sciences\, law\, journalism and various are
 as of public policy. The Academy generally encourages projects addressing 
 pressing issues of the day\, specifically naming democracy\, security\, te
 chnology and society (especially AI)\, energy including climate\, and glob
 al order. Dedicated fellowships also support projects in Jewish studies\, 
 German studies\, and public health and biotechnology. Project proposals ne
 ed not focus on Germany\, but candidates should explain how a residency in
  Berlin would enhance their work. NOT ACCEPTED: proposals in mathematics o
 r the natural sciences. NOTE FOR ARTISTS: visual artists and composers are
  invited through separate\, nomination-based competitions\, so there is no
  open application route for them here. ELIGIBILITY: fellowships are restri
 cted to citizens and permanent residents of the United States. Both emergi
 ng and established figures are eligible. PhD holders qualify as emerging s
 cholars with a strong record of peer-reviewed work beyond the dissertation
 \; candidates in non-academic fields such as journalism\, filmmaking and p
 olicy need a significant record of publication or production\; fiction and
  nonfiction writers must have published at least one book with a reputable
  press. WHAT FELLOWS DO: fellows present their work to audiences in and ar
 ound Berlin through lectures\, readings\, public discussions\, performance
 s and film screenings\, and should be willing to engage with relevant Germ
 an institutions\, organizations and the media\; these activities are integ
 ral to the Academy's mission of fostering transatlantic dialogue. APPLICAT
 ION MATERIALS: a project proposal of 1\,500 to 1\,750 words plus a one-pag
 e bibliography\; a curriculum vitae of up to 10 pages\; two writing sample
 s totalling no more than 60 pages\; and three letters of recommendation\, 
 which are due 2 October 2026. DEADLINE: Friday 25 September 2026 at 12:00 
 noon Eastern Time (18:00 Central European Time). TIMELINE: all candidates 
 are notified of the competition outcome by email in late March 2027\; the 
 2027-28 Berlin Prize recipients are announced in May 2027.\n\nOrganisation
 : American Academy in Berlin\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arn
 hold Center. RESTRICTED: fellowships are open only to citizens and permane
 nt residents of the United States.\nAward: Monthly stipend of USD 5\,000\,
  plus roundtrip airfare\, accommodation at or near the Hans Arnhold Center
 \, partial board\, in-house library services and professional networking o
 pportunities. Roughly two dozen fellowships awarded each year. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: One full academic semester (about 4 months). Fall runs
  mid-August to mid-December\; spring runs late January to late May.\n\nMor
 e: https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arnhold Center. RESTRICTED: fellows
 hips are open only to citizens and permanent residents of the United State
 s.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cannes-residence-cinema-de-demain-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: La Résidence du Festival de Cannes (Cinéma de Demain): 
 Screenwriting Residency in Paris
DESCRIPTION:La Résidence of the Festival de Cannes (part of Cinéma de Dem
 ain\, formerly La Cinéfondation) invites 12 directors each year to write 
 their screenplay in Paris. The programme provides a place of residence in 
 the heart of Paris\, a personalised programme accompanying the writing of 
 their scripts\, and a collective programme of forums with film industry pr
 ofessionals. The 12 directors from the two annual sessions present their p
 rojects at the CNC pavilion in Cannes\, giving 10-minute presentations to 
 an audience of professionals and a jury of three film industry personaliti
 es\; the CNC then awards a EUR 5\,000 grant to one director from each sess
 ion\, based on the project that most inspires the jury. The Cinef & Résid
 ence offices serve as a hub where directors meet and schedule private meet
 ings with potential producers. ELIGIBILITY: open to young filmmakers who h
 ave made one or several short films and no more than one feature film\; ca
 ndidates must NOT be residents or citizens of France. Selected filmmakers 
 must stay at the Résidence in Paris for the full session. SESSIONS: two p
 er year\, each lasting four and a half months\, the first running 15 March
  to 31 July and the second 1 October to 15 February. Artistic fields: film
 \, writing\, interdisciplinary. Deadline: 30 September 2026 at 16:00 UTC. 
 Free to apply.\n\nOrganisation: Festival de Cannes (Cinéma de Demain / La
  Résidence)\nLocation: Paris\, France. Candidates must not be residents o
 r citizens of France.\nAward: Fully supported: a place of residence in cen
 tral Paris\, a personalised script-writing programme\, and a collective pr
 ogramme of forums with film industry professionals. Directors present at t
 he CNC pavilion in Cannes\, where the CNC awards a EUR 5\,000 grant to one
  director per session. Free to apply.\nDuration: Four and a half months pe
 r session (two sessions a year)\n\nMore: https://cinemadedemain.festival-c
 annes.com/en/take-part/register-to-the-residence/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cinemadedemain.festival-cannes.com/en/take-part/register-to-the
 -residence/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France. Candidates must not be residents or citizens of Fr
 ance.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-delfina-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Delfina Foundation Residency 2027 (London
 )
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at London's Delfina Fou
 ndation\, one of the UK's best known artist-in-residence programmes\, hous
 ed at 29-31 Catherine Place near Buckingham Palace with space for 6 to 8 i
 nternational residents (own room\, shared kitchen and facilities). Delfina
  promotes artistic exchange and experiment\, offering visual artists and c
 urators a platform to carry out research\, develop ideas and position thei
 r practice within the global discourse\, with introductions to the London 
 art scene and Delfina's international network. The programme includes visi
 ts to museums\, galleries and non-profit platforms\, discussions with Lond
 on-based artists\, portfolio reviews with curators and regular networking 
 lunches\; residents are expected to take part. Applicants are not asked fo
 r a concrete project proposal but must submit a clear motivation: why they
  wish to take part\, what research they want to conduct\, and how it can c
 ontribute to Delfina's ongoing programme. WHO: visual artists and curators
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; duo appli
 cations not possible\; application must be in English. One work period ava
 ilable: 27 September to 17 December 2027. Selection by an advisory committ
 ee with a Delfina representative\; processing may exceed three months. DEA
 DLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00 Dutch time / 11:00 Caribbean
  time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Delfina Foundation\nLocation: Lon
 don\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherlands or the 
 Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subs
 idy of EUR 9\,188 for an artist or EUR 7\,232 for a curator/art observer t
 oward travel\, material and living costs (a 10 percent personal contributi
 on is automatically deducted by the Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living spac
 e and Delfina Foundation support are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. 
 Contribution for Caribbean-based artists can be increased for higher trave
 l costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 27 September to 17 D
 ecember 2027\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/g
 rants/residency/delfina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/del
 fina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:London\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherla
 nds or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-inside-out-art-museum-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Inside-Out Art Museum Residency 2027 (Bei
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at Inside-Out Art Museu
 m (IOAM) in Beijing\, one of China's leading independent platforms for con
 temporary art and research. The museum combines exhibitions\, critical inq
 uiry and public programmes\, giving residents room for in-depth research\,
  experimentation and exchange within a Chinese art scene that is otherwise
  hard to access from Europe. The residency is framed as cultural exchange 
 rather than production to deadline: IOAM works with a flexible model that 
 takes the resident's other obligations into account and sets the exact sta
 rt date in consultation with the selected candidate. WHO: visual artists\,
  curators and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of th
 e Kingdom. Duos and collaborations may apply (two artists\, two curators/c
 ritics\, or a combination who structurally make work together\, submitting
  a joint plan for the work period that leads to a single result\, and who 
 live and work together in the same space during the residency)\, but each 
 individual must submit a separate application\; the apartment is well suit
 ed to duos or partnerships. WORK PERIOD: one period of three months\, 1 Ma
 rch to 30 May 2027\, with room for one artist or duo\; you can state a pre
 ference for the work period in the application form. Selection is by advis
 ory committee\; read the Mondriaan Fund Residency explanation for the cond
 itions\, assessment and checklist\, plus the fund's general terms and cond
 itions\, before applying. DEADLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00
  Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Insi
 de-Out Art Museum\nLocation: Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curator
 s and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdo
 m\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subsidy of EUR 8\,478 for an art
 ist or EUR 5\,622 for a curator/critic toward travel\, material and living
  costs (a 10 percent personal contribution is automatically deducted by th
 e Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living space and Inside-Out Art Museum suppor
 t are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. For a selected duo the total is
  increased proportionally to cover the second applicant's travel and accom
 modation. Contribution for Caribbean-based residents can be increased for 
 higher travel costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 1 March 
 to 30 May 2027 (flexible start date\, set by IOAM in consultation with the
  resident)\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regel
 ingen/residency/inside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regelingen/residency/i
 nside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curators and critics based i
 n the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mon
 driaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:q-o2-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Q-O2: Residency Programme 2027 (Experimental Music & Soun
 d Art)
DESCRIPTION:The residencies at Q-O2 offer time and space for artistic resea
 rch\, reflection and creation in the field of experimental music and sound
  art. In 2027\, Q-O2 will host 20 residencies\, 10 for international artis
 ts and 10 for local artists living in Belgium\, working with\, on or aroun
 d sound. The programme is open to artists\, art workers and theorists who 
 wish to pursue a research-oriented project\; note that Q-O2 does not organ
 ise production-directed residencies and is not a rehearsal space. Duos are
  possible\, and exceptionally small groups too. SUPPORT: a work studio and
  materials\, a creative and communicative environment\, and the possibilit
 y to present work to a public and/or propose a workshop\; for internationa
 l residents\, accommodation in a shared apartment and a contribution to tr
 avel expenses of up to EUR 200\; and a small subsistence budget reserved f
 or artists who do not come with other funding. There is no artist fee. A f
 inal public presentation can be arranged if the artist wishes but is not e
 xpected\; what Q-O2 requires are some traces of the residency in word\, im
 age and/or audio form. APPLY by 15 September 2026: email a concise project
  proposal of no more than one page plus a permanent link to your website o
 r other secondary information (no temporary links) to info@q-o2.be with th
 e subject 'Residency27 - your name'. State where you would travel from\, h
 ow long you would like to stay (4 to 6 weeks)\, and your interest in Q-O2 
 as a working environment\, and make sure you receive an email confirmation
  of receipt.\n\nOrganisation: Q-O2 (workspace for experimental music and s
 ound art)\nLocation: Brussels\, Belgium\; 10 residencies for international
  artists and 10 for artists living in Belgium.\nAward: NO artist fee. Inte
 rnational residents: shared accommodation in the Q-O2 apartment plus a tra
 vel contribution up to EUR 200. A small subsistence budget is reserved for
  artists who do not come with other funding. Work studio\, materials and t
 echnical equipment provided. No application fee.\nDuration: Usually 3 to 6
  weeks (international applicants: 4 to 6 weeks\; stays over 4 weeks not gu
 aranteed)\n\nMore: https://www.q-o2.be/en/in-residency/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.q-o2.be/en/in-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Brussels\, Belgium\; 10 residencies for international artists and 
 10 for artists living in Belgium.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:icst-artists-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: ICST: Artists in Residence 2027 Open Call (ZHdK\, Zurich)
DESCRIPTION:The Institute for Computer Music and Sound Technology (ICST) at
  the Zurich University of the Arts (ZHdK) invites applications for its 202
 7 Artists in Residence program\, fostering artistic exchange in key areas 
 of current research. Residencies are available in five themes: Spatial Aud
 io\; Klavierautomat (algorithmic composition)\; Moving Loudspeakers\; Danc
 e and Generative AI\; and Object Performance. The program offers access to
  ICST's facilities and technical infrastructure\, professional support fro
 m researchers\, and per diems for meals and accommodation. Artists and mus
 icians working with sound and sound media\, whose practice reflects a stro
 ng interest in one of the listed research areas\, are encouraged to apply.
  One selected project from the Spatial Audio Residency will be featured at
  the SONIC MATTER Festival 2028 as part of an ongoing partnership. PRACTIC
 AL: residencies include use of facilities and technical infrastructure as 
 specified in the thematic descriptions\, plus technical support by ICST re
 search staff. Participants receive a contribution toward travel to Zurich 
 (up to CHF 300 for persons living in Europe\, up to CHF 500 for persons li
 ving outside Europe) and a per diem to cover meals and accommodation in Zu
 rich\; participants organise their own travel and accommodation\, with ICS
 T assistance if required. Residency dates are defined individually. APPLIC
 ATION: submitted via the online form\, uploading a concept sketch\, compos
 ition idea or project draft (PDF\, 2 pages\, 10 MB max)\; a portfolio of t
 hree selected works relevant to the residency topic including links to ext
 ernal audio and video (PDF\, 2 pages\, 10 MB max)\; and a tabular CV cover
 ing education and career (PDF\, 1 page\, 10 MB max). The residencies are a
 warded by a jury of ICST researchers and project leaders. TIMELINE: deadli
 ne 1 September 2026 at 24:00 CET\; candidates notified mid-October 2026. S
 elected candidates receive forms required for an invitation to Switzerland
  and must confirm participation and return completed forms within 10 days 
 or the invitation may be withdrawn.\n\nOrganisation: Institute for Compute
 r Music and Sound Technology (ICST)\, Zurich University of the Arts (ZHdK)
 \nLocation: Zurich\, Switzerland (in-person residency at ICST)\nAward: Use
  of ICST facilities and technical infrastructure plus technical support by
  research staff\; per diems for meals and accommodation during the residen
 cy\; travel contribution toward travel to Zurich (up to CHF 300 for person
 s living in Europe\, up to CHF 500 for those outside Europe). Participants
  organise their own travel and accommodation (ICST assists if required). N
 o application fee.\nDuration: Residency dates defined individually with se
 lected candidates\n\nMore: https://www.zhdk.ch/en/research/icst/icst-air/c
 onditions-selection-process-20736?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://www.zhdk.ch/en/research/icst/icst-air/conditions-selection-proc
 ess-20736?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Zurich\, Switzerland (in-person residency at ICST)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emap-emare-media-art-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Deadline: EMAP / EMARE: European Media Art Platform Residencies 202
 7
DESCRIPTION:The European Media Art Platform (EMAP/EMARE) is a network of le
 ading European media-art organisations offering fully funded two-month pro
 duction residencies for artists working with digital media\, including med
 ia art\, bio art and robotic art. Each residency provides a EUR 4\,000 gra
 nt to the applying artist (including subsistence)\, a EUR 4\,000 project b
 udget\, host-provided accommodation\, travel covered according to EU ceili
 ngs\, and access to technical facilities and media labs\; a collaborating 
 artist receives an additional EUR 2\,000 (EUR 6\,000 total for a duo). Res
 idencies take place at one of 15 host institutions across Austria\, France
 \, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, the Netherlands\, Slovenia\, Croatia\, 
 Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Poland. ELIGIBILITY
 : applicants must be EU residents or taxpayers in an EU member state\, or 
 residents/taxpayers of one of the eligible non-EU countries (Netherlands-b
 ased artists qualify). Undergraduate and Master's students are not eligibl
 e\; PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background
  may apply. IMPORTANT: applicants must apply as a duo or collective\, or p
 ropose a collaborative project\, rather than as a purely solo applicant. T
 he 2027 open call runs from 3 September 2026 to 6 November 2026 at 14:00 C
 ET. Apply online at call.emare.eu. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Eu
 ropean Media Art Platform (EMAP / EMARE)\nLocation: Two-month production r
 esidency at one of 15 host institutions across Austria\, France\, Slovakia
 \, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Slovenia\, Croatia\, Spain\, Italy\,
  Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Poland\nAward: EUR 4\,000 grant fo
 r the applying artist (including subsistence)\; EUR 2\,000 for a collabora
 ting artist (EUR 6\,000 total for a duo)\; EUR 4\,000 project budget\; acc
 ommodation provided by the host\; travel covered per EU ceilings\; access 
 to technical facilities and media labs. No application fee.\nDuration: Two
  months\n\nMore: https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Two-month production residency at one of 15 host institutions acro
 ss Austria\, France\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Sloven
 ia\, Croatia\, Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Pola
 nd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-michalski-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Jan Michalski Foundation: Writers Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Residency for writers and translators at the Jan Michalski Foun
 dation in Montricher\, Switzerland\, set in seven distinctive 'cabin' modu
 les hanging from an openwork canopy\, offering conditions to start\, conti
 nue or finish a writing project. Around forty authors from around the worl
 d (emerging to established) are hosted each year. Open to all kinds of wri
 ting and all languages\, with priority given to literary writers and trans
 lators\; other disciplines are welcome as long as literature is at the hea
 rt of the project. Residencies are for individuals or pairs working on a c
 ommon project (e.g. a writer and a translator). A percentage of residencie
 s are dedicated to nature writing. WHAT IS PROVIDED: a private cabin for i
 ndependent living (a separate cabin per person for pairs\; one accessible 
 cabin for reduced mobility)\, travel costs to and from home\, a weekly all
 owance of CHF 400\, breakfast and lunch\, electric bikes\, and daytime lib
 rary access. ELIGIBILITY: no age or nationality restrictions\; beginners a
 ccepted\; one application per year\; former residents may not reapply (fam
 ilies\, children and pets cannot be accommodated). Stays cannot be split i
 nto multiple periods. Selection is by a panel chaired by Vera Michalski-Ho
 ffmann\, assessing the literary quality of the project\, the candidate's b
 ackground\, and whether the stay length matches the project scope. APPLICA
 TION: online in English or French (work excerpts may be in any language)\;
  the 2027 form is open 2 June to 31 August 2026\; selected candidates anno
 unced December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Jan Michalski Foundation for Writing
  and Literature\nLocation: Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lau
 sanne and Geneva)\nAward: Weekly allowance of CHF 400\, plus travel costs 
 to and from home covered\, accommodation in a private cabin\, and breakfas
 t and lunch provided. Electric bikes and library access included.\nDuratio
 n: Two weeks to three months (first 2027 residents arrive mid-January 2027
 )\n\nMore: https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lausanne and Geneva)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-residency-fundaziun-nairs-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260912
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Residency at Fundaziun Nairs 2026
DESCRIPTION:Stichting Stokroos funds a three-month reflective residency at 
 Fundaziun Nairs in Scuol\, Switzerland\, for one selected visual artist\, 
 designer or craft practitioner (overlap possible). Both emerging and estab
 lished makers may apply. Stokroos covers full accommodation and meals dire
 ctly with Fundaziun Nairs and provides a discretionary EUR 7\,000 budget f
 or living\, travel and production. The application should include a propos
 al that engages specifically with the residency\, its Alpine surroundings 
 and/or its historical and cultural context. Eligibility: you completed you
 r first subject-specific (vocational or higher) programme in 2022 or earli
 er\, or have an equivalent established practice\, or started without forma
 l training (first presentation marks the start of your practice)\; at leas
 t 21 years old\; living and working in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (inc
 luding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; not curren
 tly enrolled in a study or post-academic programme. Applications are indiv
 idual only\; duos and collectives cannot apply. Makers already selected by
  Fundaziun Nairs may still apply if they meet the criteria. You may submit
  only one application per year across all Stokroos grants\, and must not h
 ave received a Seed Grant rejection in the previous calendar year. Apply v
 ia the online form (Dutch or English) with a portfolio PDF up to 20 pages\
 , optional video up to 10 minutes total\, CV up to 2 pages\, and work/plan
  descriptions up to 2\,500 characters each. Selection includes an introduc
 tory interview with up to three candidates\; Stokroos aims to respond with
 in 8 weeks. No appeal is possible. Application window: 1 to 11 September 2
 026. More information at nairs.ch.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLo
 cation: Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.\nAward: Fully supported stay (accommodation and 
 meals paid directly to Fundaziun Nairs) plus an unrestricted living\, trav
 el and production budget of EUR 7\,000. 80% paid before the residency\, th
 e remainder on receipt of a brief final report. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Intensive three-month working period (July through September).\n\nMor
 e: https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.
END:VEVENT
