UID:ses12naus-two-phase-residency-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fundacion Ses12naus: Two-Phase Residency for Visual Artis
 ts and Curators\, Ibiza (2026-2027)
DESCRIPTION:Ses12naus\, a non-profit founded in 2016 to strengthen the cult
 ural and artistic fabric of Ibiza and develop the island as an internation
 al reference for contemporary artistic creation\, is launching a two-phase
  residency for visual artists and curators at any career stage. Four proje
 cts are selected for the 2026-2027 edition: two by artists or curators bas
 ed in the Balearic Islands\, one from the rest of Spain and one from anoth
 er European country. STRUCTURE: Phase 1 (21 November to 13 December 2026) 
 is dedicated to research and exploration of the territory and an in-depth 
 understanding of the local context\, with a required public activity linke
 d to the process\; between phases the Foundation's team actively follows u
 p on the conceptualisation and formalisation of the proposal\; in Phase 2 
 (17 May to 7 June 2027) residents return to produce and present: artists p
 roduce their works\, curators continue their research\, and both present r
 esults. The format supports developing a new project or giving continuity 
 to an ongoing one\, in dialogue with Ibiza and its communities. FUNDING: E
 UR 1\,800 honorarium plus EUR 300 public-activity fee per resident\; trave
 l up to EUR 330 (Spain) or EUR 770 (Europe) booked by the Foundation (no t
 ravel between phases is financed)\; production up to EUR 3\,000 for artist
 s plus EUR 500 installation and EUR 200 public-activity costs (curators: E
 UR 500 plus EUR 200). RESOURCES: private bedroom and bathroom with shared 
 kitchen and living room\, a workspace at La Carpinteria sized to the proje
 ct with projectors\, speakers\, machinery and tools (specific materials no
 t in the inventory come from the production budget)\, production assistanc
 e\, a shared car for the duration (valid driving licence required) and air
 port transfers. APPLICATION: online form\, deadline 30 September 2026\, 23
 :59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Fundacion Ses12naus\nLocation: Ibiza\, Balearic 
 Islands\, Spain (at La Carpinteria creation centre\, Can Bufi). Open to vi
 sual artists and curators residing in the Balearic Islands\, Spain and Eur
 ope: of four selected projects\, two go to the Balearic Islands\, one to t
 he rest of Spain and one to another European country. No age limit.\nAward
 : Honorarium of EUR 1\,800 per resident (EUR 900 per phase) plus EUR 300 f
 or the public activity (all subject to taxes and withholdings). Travel up 
 to EUR 330 for participants from Spain or EUR 770 from other European coun
 tries (booked by the Foundation). Production: artists up to EUR 3\,000 for
  production and public presentation (including transport of the work)\, pl
 us up to EUR 500 installation costs and EUR 200 for public activities\; cu
 rators up to EUR 500 for the final presentation and EUR 200 for the public
  activity. Also included: private bedroom with private bathroom\, shared k
 itchen and living room\, workspace at La Carpinteria with technical resour
 ces\, production assistance\, a shared car (driving licence required) and 
 airport transfers. Free to apply.\nDuration: Two 3-week phases: 21 Novembe
 r to 13 December 2026 (research and territory exploration\, with a public 
 activity) and 17 May to 7 June 2027 (production and presentation)\, with a
 ctive follow-up between phases\n\nMore: https://ses12naus.org/en/applicati
 on-form-open-call-2026-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://ses12naus.org/en/application-form-open-call-2026-2027/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ibiza\, Balearic Islands\, Spain (at La Carpinteria creation centr
 e\, Can Bufi). Open to visual artists and curators residing in the Baleari
 c Islands\, Spain and Europe: of four selected projects\, two go to the Ba
 learic Islands\, one to the rest of Spain and one to another European coun
 try. No age limit.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpzimmer-open-call-collectives-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
SUMMARY:Deadline: wpZimmer: Open Call 2027 residencies for collectives (Ant
 werp)
DESCRIPTION:wpZimmer\, the Antwerp arts workspace structurally supported by
  the Flemish Government\, offers four five-week residencies in 2027 for co
 llectives of artists and artworkers\, realized in partnership with C-TAKT.
  WHAT YOU GET: a EUR 5\,000 (excl. VAT) financial contribution per collect
 ive (budget managed by the collective)\, two workspaces (a technically equ
 ipped studio of approx. 18m x 17m and a medium atelier of approx. 4m x 13m
  suited to physical practices)\, shared accommodation for up to 6 people\,
  and access to wpZimmer's community and knowledge in a reciprocal working 
 relationship. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: existing\, new or temporary collectives of 
 at least 3 artists or artworkers (anyone working in a creative field)\, wi
 th at least one member living or working in Belgium\; you can even dedicat
 e the residency to building a collective. THE PRACTICE SHOULD BE: an exper
 iment with collectivity and collective practices\; process-oriented rather
  than single-project\; not reliant on one discipline or medium\; bringing 
 people together in non-traditional ways beyond the black box or white cube
 . SELECTION: external jury of Tine Colen\, Sezen Atmaca and Katinka de Jon
 ge with the wpZimmer team\, judging only the application text (max 600 wor
 ds on the criteria)\; answer expected in November 2026. DEADLINE: 20 Septe
 mber 2026\, 23:59 CET\; the form is capped at 100 applications\, so apply 
 early. Applications in English or Dutch via the form on the website only (
 not email).\n\nOrganisation: wpZimmer\nLocation: Antwerp\, Belgium. At lea
 st one member of the collective must be living or working in Belgium.\nAwa
 rd: EUR 5\,000 (excl. VAT) financial contribution per collective\, managed
  by the collective\, plus a five-week residency with two workspaces (a tec
 hnically equipped studio of approx. 18m x 17m and a medium atelier of appr
 ox. 4m x 13m adapted to physical practices) and shared accommodation for u
 p to 6 people. Four collectives selected. No application fee.\nDuration: F
 ive-week residency slots in 2027: 15 March to 18 April\, 17 May to 20 June
 \, 10 October to 12 November\, or 22 November to 24 December\n\nMore: http
 s://wpzimmer.be/en/open-call/open-call-2027-2/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://wpzimmer.be/en/open-call/open-call-2027-2/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Antwerp\, Belgium. At least one member of the collective must be l
 iving or working in Belgium.
END:VEVENT
