BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-jatiwangi-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Jatiwangi art Fact
 ory 2027 (Indonesia)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect or spatial practitioner for 
 a two-month residency in 2027 at Jatiwangi art Factory (JaF)\, an internat
 ionally recognised artistic collective based in a former roof tile factory
  in West Java\, Indonesia. Jatiwangi's history is closely bound up with th
 e colonial history of Indonesia: the Dutch government built large roof til
 e factories in the region in the early twentieth century\, turning it into
  the most important centre of roof tile production in Southeast Asia. Now 
 that this industry has largely disappeared\, JaF develops new visions for 
 the changing rural area with clay and community empowerment at their heart
 . The residency is part of Tahun Tanah\, a recurring programme on the rela
 tionship between the people of Jatiwangi and the region's history of clay 
 and terracotta civilisation\; the 2027 theme is Elmu Ning Tanah (Learning 
 from the Earth). As resident you explore with the local community what tan
 ah (earth) means in this area\, not only as a material for the terracotta 
 industry but also as a carrier of history\, memory and culture\, and you h
 elp shape a future for the terracotta industry rooted in local knowledge\,
  traditions and the needs of the community. ELIGIBILITY: you are an indivi
 dual designer\, architect or spatial practitioner\; you are established in
  the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Si
 nt Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands)\; you are registered in the busine
 ss register of the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) or another business reg
 ister within the Kingdom of the Netherlands\; and you have had a professio
 nal practice in the creative industry for at least four years. NOT open to
  duos\, collectives or cooperative ventures\, nor to designers and makers 
 who receive a grant during the work period under the Talent Development Gr
 ant Scheme\, the Open Call Self-taught Designer or the Open Call Emerging 
 Design Practices ABCSSS\; accepting this open call means you cannot apply 
 to those schemes and open calls in 2027. FUNDING: EUR 4\,500 subsidy for t
 he two-month residency\; accommodation at JaF is a small private container
  house with two single beds and a bathroom/toilet. Assessment takes the fo
 rm of a tender: an external advisory committee ranks proposals on the arti
 stic quality of the work\, the quality of the proposed project and the mot
 ivation in relation to the goals of the residency\, and the highest-scorin
 g proposals are awarded. Decision within eight weeks of the closing date. 
 Submit via the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026\, 16:00 CEST
 .\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industr
 ies Fund NL) in collaboration with Jatiwangi art Factory\, Indonesia\nLoca
 tion: Residency takes place at Jatiwangi art Factory in Jatiwangi\, West J
 ava\, Indonesia. Applicants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba
 \, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of t
 he Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the Kingdom o
 f the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 4\,500 subsidy for a two-month residency\, 
 paid by the Creative Industries Fund NL. Accommodation at Jatiwangi art Fa
 ctory is provided: a small private container house furnished with two sing
 le beds and a bathroom/toilet. No application fee.\nDuration: Two months i
 n 2027\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-resid
 ency-jatiwangi-art-factory?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-jatiwang
 i-art-factory?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Jatiwangi art Factory in Jatiwangi\, West
  Java\, Indonesia. Applicants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aru
 ba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of
  the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the Kingdom
  of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-suriname-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Suriname 2027 (Par
 amaribo\, Moengo\, Frederiksdorp)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect or interdisciplinary maker f
 or a three-month residency in 2027 across three locations in Suriname: Par
 amaribo\, Moengo and Frederiksdorp\, each with its own cultural\, historic
 al and social context. The residency is inspired by the Surinamese notion 
 of alakondre (literally 'all countries')\, which symbolises living togethe
 r in cultural diversity and emphasises the power of coexisting differences
 . Rather than simply promoting harmony\, alakondre acknowledges historical
  inequalities\, cultural sensitivities and tensions ensuing from colonial 
 and socio-economic realities\, which demands openness and critical awarene
 ss of your position as a creative practitioner\; personal stories\, whethe
 r family history or questions of identity\, can provide powerful entry poi
 nts. A network of local partners supports the residency\, and at each loca
 tion a local maker selected by Surinamese partner organisations works alon
 gside you\, creating natural opportunities for creative exchange and dialo
 gue. ELIGIBILITY: you are an individual designer\, architect or spatial pr
 actitioner\; you are established in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (the Ne
 therlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maar
 ten)\; you are registered in the register of the Dutch Chamber of Commerce
  (KvK) or another business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands\
 ; and you have run a professional practice within the creative industries 
 for at least four years. NOT open to duos\, collectives or collaborative p
 artnerships\, nor to current recipients of the Talent Development Grant Sc
 heme\, the Open Call Self-taught Designer or the Open Call Emerging Design
  Practices ABCSSS\; accepting this open call means you cannot apply to tho
 se schemes and open calls in 2027. FUNDING: EUR 8\,500 subsidy for the thr
 ee-month residency\; one position is awarded. Assessment takes the form of
  a tender: an external advisory committee ranks proposals on the artistic 
 quality of the work\, the quality of the development plan and the motivati
 on in relation to the residency's objective\, and the highest-scoring prop
 osal is awarded. Decision within eight weeks of the closing date. Submit v
 ia the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026\, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund
  NL) with local partner organisations in Suriname\nLocation: Residency tak
 es place at three locations in Suriname: Paramaribo\, Moengo and Frederiks
 dorp. Applicants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\
 , Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherla
 nds) and registered in a business register within the Kingdom of the Nethe
 rlands.\nAward: EUR 8\,500 subsidy for a three-month residency\, paid by t
 he Creative Industries Fund NL. One residency position is awarded. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: Three months in 2027\, moving between Paramaribo\,
  Moengo and Frederiksdorp\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gra
 nts/open-call-residency-suriname?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-suriname
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at three locations in Suriname: Paramaribo\,
  Moengo and Frederiksdorp. Applicants must be established in the Netherlan
 ds\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Ki
 ngdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the
  Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-think-tanger-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Think Tanger 2027 
 (Tangier\, Morocco)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect\, spatial practitioner or ma
 ker for a two-month residency in 2027 at Think Tanger\, a multidisciplinar
 y cultural platform dedicated to stimulating culture\, creativity\, innova
 tion and exchange in Tangier\, Morocco. Founded in 2016\, Think Tanger uni
 tes artists\, designers\, researchers\, entrepreneurs and local communitie
 s to explore the urban and cultural dynamics of a city in transformation a
 nd to promote understanding and dialogue\, working through alternative edu
 cation\, creative entrepreneurship\, art production and participatory rese
 arch. The residency was set up with the Fund to stimulate crossovers and e
 xperiments\, initiate exchanges and learn from other people's perspectives
 \, knowledge and ideas. It offers the opportunity to carry out research\, 
 expand your network and develop new work with a focus on design\, urbanism
  and socio-spatial dynamics\, creatively researching existing presuppositi
 ons and social issues in Tangier's unique urban context. ELIGIBILITY: you 
 are an individual designer\, architect\, spatial practitioner or maker\; y
 ou are established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\,
  Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands)\; you are reg
 istered in the business register of the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) or
  another business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands\; and you
  have had a professional practice in the creative industry for at least tw
 o years (note: a lower bar than the four years required by the Fund's othe
 r 2027 residencies). NOT open to duos\, collectives or cooperative venture
 s\, nor to designers and makers who receive a grant during the work period
  under the Talent Development Grant Scheme\, the Open Call Self-taught Des
 igner or the Open Call Emerging Design Practices ABCSSS\; accepting this o
 pen call means you cannot apply to those schemes and open calls in 2027. F
 UNDING: EUR 5\,500 subsidy for the two-month residency. Assessment takes t
 he form of a tender: an external advisory committee ranks proposals on the
  artistic quality of the work\, the quality of the proposed project and th
 e motivation in relation to the goals of the residency\, and the highest-s
 coring proposal is awarded. Decision within eight weeks of the closing dat
 e. Submit via the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026\, 16:00 C
 EST.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Indu
 stries Fund NL) in collaboration with Think Tanger\, Morocco\nLocation: Re
 sidency takes place at Think Tanger in Tangier\, Morocco. Applicants must 
 be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sin
 t Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in
  a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\
 ,500 subsidy for a two-month residency\, paid by the Creative Industries F
 und NL. No application fee.\nDuration: Two months in 2027\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-think-tanger?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-think-ta
 nger?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Think Tanger in Tangier\, Morocco. Applic
 ants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, 
 Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and reg
 istered in a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
