DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:Deadline: Institut francais x Cite internationale des arts Residenc
 y 2027 (Paris)
DESCRIPTION:The Institut francais' flagship international residency line at
  the Cite internationale des arts in Paris: around 70 live-in studios a ye
 ar for artists and cultural professionals across 15 disciplines\, from vis
 ual arts\, film\, music\, dance and literature to architecture\, fashion a
 nd gastronomy. WHAT YOU GET: a live-in studio in the Marais or Montmartre 
 covered by the Institut francais\, with a residency grant of at least EUR 
 1\,100 per month plus travel\, insurance and visa costs funded by the part
 ner organization that nominates you. ELIGIBILITY: professional artists per
 manently residing outside France for at least five years\, free of obligat
 ions during the residency\, with working French and/or English. IMPORTANT:
  you apply through a supporting partner (local Institut francais\, embassy
  cultural service or cultural organization)\, not directly\; contact your 
 local branch before the deadline. DEADLINE: 8 October 2026 for residencies
  of 3\, 6 or 9 months starting between April 2027 and April 2028.\n\nOrgan
 isation: Institut francais and Cite internationale des arts\nLocation: Par
 is\, France. Open worldwide to artists who have lived outside France for a
 t least five years\; applications go through a partner organization (Insti
 tut francais network\, cultural institutions)\, not directly.\nAward: Resi
 dency grant of minimum EUR 1\,100 per month funded by the nominating partn
 er\, plus international travel\, insurance and visa costs\; the Institut f
 rancais covers the monthly costs of the live-in studio (25 to 40 m2). Arou
 nd 70 places. No application fee.\nDuration: 3\, 6 or 9 months between Apr
 il 2027 and April 2028\n\nMore: https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/e
 n/appels-a-candidature/institut-francais-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/en/appels-a-candidature/instit
 ut-francais-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France. Open worldwide to artists who have lived outside F
 rance for at least five years\; applications go through a partner organiza
 tion (Institut francais network\, cultural institutions)\, not directly.
END:VEVENT
