UID:hiap-usrp-ukraine-solidarity-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: HIAP: Ukraine Solidarity Residencies Programme 2027 (Finl
 and)
DESCRIPTION:The Ukraine Solidarity Residencies Programme (USRP)\, run by HI
 AP with partner residencies and supported by the Finnish Ministry of Educa
 tion and Culture\, offers residencies across Finland for professional Ukra
 inian or Ukraine-based artists and arts practitioners affected by the war\
 , whether still in Ukraine or based elsewhere. WHAT YOU GET: a working gra
 nt of EUR 1\,200 per month\, free living and working space\, one return tr
 ip from the artist's home\, and a small access budget for disabled artists
 . HOSTS: HIAP Suomenlinna in Helsinki (families welcome)\, AARK in the Tur
 ku Archipelago (families welcome)\, Art Centre Salmela in Mantyharju\, eco
  art residency Fairres in Porvoo\, Nelimarkka Artist Residency in Alajarvi
 \, Vartsila Art House in North Karelia (prioritises artists with families)
  and Gjutars Artists House in Vantaa\; some hosts take up to four people i
 ncluding family members\, and applicants state their preferred location an
 d length in the form. ELIGIBILITY: professional Ukrainian or Ukraine-based
  artists and arts practitioners from all disciplines\, affected by the war
  in Ukraine. APPLICATION: in English via the online form only (hiap.fi/usr
 p-application-form)\; professional background and current situation (up to
  250 words or 2 minutes each\, text\, audio or video accepted) and a portf
 olio link of up to 10 pages or 5 minutes\; access requirements can be shar
 ed confidentially. DEADLINE: 2 November 2026\, 15:00 (GMT+2)\; jury meets 
 in November.\n\nOrganisation: HIAP (Helsinki International Artist Programm
 e) and partner residencies\nLocation: Seven residencies across Finland: HI
 AP Suomenlinna (Helsinki)\, AARK (Korpo\, Turku Archipelago)\, Art Centre 
 Salmela (Mantyharju)\, Fairres (Porvoo)\, Nelimarkka Artist Residency (Ala
 jarvi)\, Vartsila Art House (North Karelia) and Gjutars Artists House (Van
 taa). Open to Ukrainian or Ukraine-based artists.\nAward: Working grant of
  EUR 1\,200 per month (EUR 1\,200 to 3\,600 depending on residency length)
 \, plus free living and working space\, one return trip from the artist's 
 home\, and a small access budget for disabled artists. No application fee.
 \nDuration: 1 to 3 months (extension possible)\, between January and July 
 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.hiap.fi/open-call/open-call-for-ukrainian-and-u
 kraine-based-artists-in-finland-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.hiap.fi/open-call/open-call-for-ukrainian-and-ukraine-based
 -artists-in-finland-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Seven residencies across Finland: HIAP Suomenlinna (Helsinki)\, AA
 RK (Korpo\, Turku Archipelago)\, Art Centre Salmela (Mantyharju)\, Fairres
  (Porvoo)\, Nelimarkka Artist Residency (Alajarvi)\, Vartsila Art House (N
 orth Karelia) and Gjutars Artists House (Vantaa). Open to Ukrainian or Ukr
 aine-based artists.
END:VEVENT
