UID:bom-dia-oasis-cultivamos-cultura-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Bom Dia OASis Residency 2027 (Cultivamos Cultura\, Portug
 al)
DESCRIPTION:Cultivamos Cultura\, the art-science and bioart organisation in
  rural Sao Luis (Odemira\, Portugal)\, hosts the Bom Dia residency as part
  of the OASis programme. One selected proposal (individual or a group of u
 p to two people\, same conditions) spends 7 to 30 days in March 2027 produ
 cing an artwork that joins the OASis group exhibition in 2027\, is shown l
 ocally and across the OASis network\, and leaves one output in the Cultiva
 mos Cultura collection. SUPPORT: project grant of EUR 1\,300\; travel budg
 et up to EUR 500\; production and material costs up to EUR 1\,600 (approve
 d before purchase\, paid on invoice)\; daily food allowance\; private room
  in a shared farmhouse with shared kitchen\; studio and free access to all
  Cultivamos Cultura spaces and resources. ELIGIBILITY: international artis
 ts\, creators and researchers from any field\, including practitioners wor
 king between culture and other disciplines. ASSESSMENT PRIORITIES: use of 
 local or natural materials\, strong ecological interest\, care for a susta
 inable future\, community interaction\, and exchange with international ar
 tists. OBLIGATIONS: stay on site for the whole approved period\, engage th
 e local community (artist talks\, walks\, workshops or open studios)\, and
  create an output for the 2027 exhibition and the collection\; travel beyo
 nd the village means renting a car from the production grant. APPLY with a
  project statement (max 500 words) with images\, an estimated resources li
 st\, a signed declaration of originality\, portfolio or website plus short
  CV (max 4 pages)\, a timeline\, and five images for communication. DEADLI
 NE: 30 October 2026 at 18:00 CET\, or earlier if 100 applications are rece
 ived first\; results in the third week of December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: 
 Cultivamos Cultura (OASis / European OASIS project)\nLocation: Sao Luis\, 
 Odemira\, Portugal (rural Alentejo\; private room in a shared farmhouse). 
 Open internationally\; the local community mostly speaks Portuguese.\nAwar
 d: Project grant of EUR 1\,300\, travel budget up to EUR 500\, production 
 and material costs up to EUR 1\,600 (pre-approved\, paid on invoice)\, dai
 ly food allowance\, private room in a shared farmhouse\, and a studio for 
 the whole period. No application fee.\nDuration: 7 to 30 days in March 202
 7\, plus participation in the OASis group exhibition in 2027.\n\nMore: htt
 ps://cultivamoscultura.com/2026/09/17/bom-dia-oasis-residency-call-for-202
 7/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cultivamoscultura.com/2026/09/17/bom-dia-oasis-residency-call-f
 or-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sao Luis\, Odemira\, Portugal (rural Alentejo\; private room in a 
 shared farmhouse). Open internationally\; the local community mostly speak
 s Portuguese.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:invisible-cartographies-buinho-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: Invisible Cartographies: Residency for Neurodivergent Art
 ists (Buinho\, Portugal)
DESCRIPTION:Part of the Creative Europe project Invisible Cartographies (Bu
 inho with FabLab Cuenca\, Spain\, and the Veljko Ramadanovic School\, Serb
 ia)\, which creates sensory cartographies of public spaces\, schools and m
 useums with neurodivergent communities. Two artists live in Messejana for 
 six weeks (11 January to 21 February 2027) and work with students of the A
 grupamento de Escolas de Aljustrel\; proposals should sketch what you want
  to investigate and how you might work with the school community\, and nee
 d not be a finished plan. SUPPORT: EUR 1\,200 artist fee\, free accommodat
 ion\, travel budget up to EUR 300\, production budget\, and access to Buin
 ho's FabLab. ELIGIBILITY: preference for neurodivergent artists\; self-ide
 ntification is enough\, no diagnosis or documentation required\; applicant
 s must commit to the full period and\, if selected\, provide a criminal-re
 cord certificate for work with minors. APPLICATION: online in English or P
 ortuguese\; written answers (500-word expression of interest\, 750-word pr
 oposal) or audio/video recordings (5 and 7 minutes) assessed equally\; por
 tfolio by link or upload (under 10 MB)\; access rider and consent sections
  included. Questions and access needs: info@buinho.pt. NOTE: this funded c
 all is separate from Buinho's regular paid residencies\; two further calls
  (Cuenca\, Belgrade) are announced but not yet open. DEADLINE: 26 October 
 2026\, 23:59 Lisbon time.\n\nOrganisation: Buinho Creative Hub (Creative E
 urope project Invisible Cartographies)\nLocation: Messejana\, Alentejo\, P
 ortugal (full-period stay\; work with the Aljustrel school community).\nAw
 ard: EUR 1\,200 artist fee for the six weeks\, free accommodation for the 
 full period\, travel budget up to EUR 300\, plus a production budget and F
 abLab access. Meals not included. No application fee.\nDuration: Two funde
 d six-week residencies\, 11 January to 21 February 2027.\n\nMore: https://
 www.invisiblecartographies.eu/open-calls?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.invisiblecartographies.eu/open-calls?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Messejana\, Alentejo\, Portugal (full-period stay\; work with the 
 Aljustrel school community).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creart-lublin-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T231546Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261023
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261024
SUMMARY:Deadline: CreArt 3.0: Artist Residency in Lublin 2026
DESCRIPTION:The City of Lublin and Warsztaty Kultury host a 17-day CreArt 3
 .0 residency for two artists (one from Lublin\, one from another CreArt ne
 twork city) who develop a joint project based on a 1.5-metre movable globe
  originally made for the Planet Lublin installation\, to be presented in L
 ublin's public space. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 800 gross grant per artist (paid w
 ithin 21 days after the residency\; 20 percent income tax reduction for ar
 tists from abroad)\, up to EUR 460 gross production budget\, and\, for art
 ists from CreArt cities\, flights to Warsaw or Lublin\, accommodation and 
 two meals a day (Warsaw to Lublin transfer at the artist's own cost). ELIG
 IBILITY: individual artists (no groups) born or residing in a CreArt netwo
 rk city\, HDLU members\, or Ukrainian artists via the Lviv Artistic Counci
 l Dialogue\; an arts degree or equivalent documented track record is requi
 red\; no age limit\; a European Health Insurance Card or equivalent is req
 uired. Application: one English PDF (ID\, proof of network-city connection
 \, CV\, portfolio\, project proposal) via the CreArt website. Results by 3
 0 October 2026. An English final report of at least 6 pages is due afterwa
 rds. DEADLINE: 23 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: City of Lublin and Warszt
 aty Kultury (CreArt network)\nLocation: Lublin\, Poland. Open to artists b
 orn or residing in a CreArt network city (Kaunas\, Liepaja\, Skopje\, Avei
 ro\, Valladolid\, Lublin\, Venice\, Clermont-Ferrand\, Rouen\, Regensburg\
 , Ceske Budejovice\, Oulu)\, plus HDLU members (Croatia) and Ukrainian art
 ists via the Lviv Artistic Council Dialogue.\nAward: EUR 800 gross grant p
 er artist plus up to EUR 460 gross for materials and production\; flights\
 , accommodation and two meals a day covered for artists from CreArt networ
 k cities. No application fee.\nDuration: 17-day residency\, 12 to 28 Novem
 ber 2026\, with a public presentation in Lublin on 27 November.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://creart2-eu.org/open-calls/open-call-creart-3-0-artist-residency-pro
 gram-in-lublin-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://creart2-eu.org/open-calls/open-call-creart-3-0-artist-residency
 -program-in-lublin-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
LOCATION:Lublin\, Poland. Open to artists born or residing in a CreArt netw
 ork city (Kaunas\, Liepaja\, Skopje\, Aveiro\, Valladolid\, Lublin\, Venic
 e\, Clermont-Ferrand\, Rouen\, Regensburg\, Ceske Budejovice\, Oulu)\, plu
